@NAME@ experimental Linux x86_64 package

This is an unverified test artifact for the Ubuntu 24.04 glibc baseline.
Read VERSION for the source revisions and build profile. The host must provide
the libraries listed in HOST-LIBRARIES, graphics drivers, fonts and CA trust.
CPU requirements follow the Engine build. Developer builds use the build
machine's instruction set by default; the x86_64 label alone does not promise
compatibility with other CPUs. Verify a portable baseline before redistribution.
Rust crate and bundled font license notices are incomplete. Resolve these and
verify the full browser in a runtime-only environment before redistributing it.

From this extracted folder, launch:

  ./@EXECUTABLE@ https://example.org/

Linux uses CPU page painting by default; the shell still draws with the GPU.
PHOTON_ENABLE_GPU_PAINTING=1 enables experimental Vulkan page painting. It
produced blank content on the tested AMD/RADV host; the failing GPU stage has
not been isolated. Keep the default for the supported experimental configuration.

Register the application menu entry and web URL handlers:

  ./bin/@PRODUCT@-desktop install

Registration does not change the default browser. Choose @NAME@ explicitly in
your desktop settings. Paths containing spaces work. Registration rejects
quotes, backticks, dollar signs, backslashes, percent signs and control bytes.

Updates are manual. Quit the browser and its helpers, extract the new version
beside this folder, then run the new version's desktop installer. Keep this
folder for application rollback, but a newer profile may not work with an old
version. Back up your data before testing experimental updates.

To remove this installation, choose another default browser if needed, run:

  ./bin/@PRODUCT@-desktop uninstall

Then delete this extracted folder. An old version cannot unregister a newer
one. Removal preserves browsing data and settings at:

  ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/@DATA_FOLDER@/Default
  ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/@DATA_FOLDER@/config.toml

Development and packaged versions share those paths by default. Use an isolated
PHOTON_PROFILE_DIR for evaluation. Do not launch a second process on the same
profile; single-instance URL handoff is not implemented yet.
